WEBVTT

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:32.280
.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.400
Come on!

00:02:33.840 --> 00:03:00.000
We'll be right back.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.750
I don't know.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.600
Come on.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:55.380
*music*

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.840
I'm sorry.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.430
I want to see you as soon as you get through college.

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.430
All I keep this count is very valuable.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:44.230
I want to see you as soon as you get through college.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:45.430
You have what it takes.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.130
We need your spare to buy business.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.430
I have a big future for you.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.130
You cannot take it.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:49.930
Don't forget it.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:50.430
Who are you?

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:51.430
I didn't quite catch the road.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.130
I may not look just like you, but I may have opportunity.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:54.680
Oh.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.360
Well, I... I should say I do remember.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:21.990
I should certainly hope to kiss a pig if I didn't.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:22.990
Thank you.

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:24.000
Now let me see.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.000
That was football, wasn't it?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.000
It wasn't ice hockey.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.010
I go to everything.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.330
Football, Mr. Wagleberry.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.890
Football, of course.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.830
And I presume I promised you a job.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:36.090
I usually do when I get excited.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:36.950
Oh.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.610
But you shall have it.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.940
With me, your promise is a sacred pledge.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:42.280
My word is my bond.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.530
My handshake is like a certified check.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:45.800
My check is like a...

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.520
He who loses honor loses everything.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:49.160
Right.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.990
We don't start people at the top, you understand.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:52.970
That would be too easy.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.080
We do it the American way.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.290
We give them an opportunity to work up from the bottom.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:09:59.780
What satisfaction.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.610
What a feeling of accomplishment you will have

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.450
when you were able to look back from whatever rung of the ladder

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:08.170
your go-gettiveness would have placed you upon and say,

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.600
I, I did that.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.020
Yes, sir.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:12.560
Fine.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.260
You know nothing about the advertising business at all, I presume?

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.160
Well, I, uh...

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:18.640
Good!

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.500
Then you won't have anything to unlearn.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.040
You'll be able to start right in the basement,

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.660
and your rise will be all the more spectacular.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.250
Every man is the architect of his own fortune.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:29.910
Excellent.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.480
I have ideas.

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:34.030
You could almost say bursting with them.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:34.790
But contain them.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:35.390
Save them.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:37.450
Don't squirt them all out at once.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.510
The idea department is a little congested at the moment.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:41.890
It always is, for that matter.

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.610
There never seems to be any shortage of...

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.750
Oh, but that would only depress you.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.750
I'll tell you what I'm going to do for you.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:52.510
I'm going to find you a little nook in the bookkeeping department.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:53.970
A regular little niche.

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:55.650
You could almost call it a cranny.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:57.710
The rest will depend upon you.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.000
Well, thank you very much, but...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.240
these ideas how i envy you this chance you're receiving today my my father unfortunately left

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:12.320
me the business oh just one of those things you have no personal fortune i hope well no sir i uh

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:18.160
great and probably only the closure stand in well not exactly i mean this isn't my other suit oh

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:24.730
isn't it no well no matter clothes do not make the man on the contrary as shatner said to marks

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.040
It's man who makes the clothes!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.000
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.230
- Is it Bill, Doc? - Yes, will you?

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:49.410
- I'd like to see you. - Oh, me?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:53.040
Oh, by the way.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:28.070
Come in.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:49.360
You want to see me, Chief?

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.980
- Yes, I'm sorry to say I do, Harold.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.360
- Oh.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:20.170
- How long have you been with us, Dittleboss?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:23.460
- About 20 years, I guess, 22 years.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.730
- Too long.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.430
- Why, it seems like yesterday to me.

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:28.220
I mean that I started here.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.000
- Well, it was quite a few yesterdays ago.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.900
The earth has cooled considerably since you put on your first pair of sleeve protectors

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:34.900
outside there.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:37.400
Yes, I guess it has.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:41.220
And so have you, Harold, so have you.

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:43.400
I don't know exactly what you're talking about.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.080
I may be a little older, but I'm quite sure that I...

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.240
I had great hopes for you, little Bart.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:52.420
If ever I saw a promising type of American youth, full of zing, full of zest, full of

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:53.420
zowie, it was you.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:58.080
I remember that day I first saw you, the bases were full, the crowd was breathless.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.000
You strutted up to the plate, swinging through.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.840
three bats at once.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:02.600
- What?

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.510
- Oh no, it was hockey, wasn't it?

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:05.790
Ice hockey, of course.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:08.050
You got the puck, ain't it?

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:08.890
- It wasn't?

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:11.200
- Well, what does it matter anyway at this point?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.740
A man is only as young as his arteries, Harold,

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:16.340
and a firm is only as young as its employees.

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:18.460
My father fired anyone who got to be 50.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:20.800
Man, woman, or child, it didn't matter to him.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:24.240
That was his motto, the cornerstone of its success.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:25.640
Personally, I found the method harsh.

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:26.940
I do not subscribe to it.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.280
With me, a man is as young as his ideas.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.850
Yes, sir.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:34.530
I even participated in, or at least closed my eyes to,

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:37.230
a small deception some of the older employees practiced.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:37.610
When?

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.030
Because my father was extremely nearsighted,

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.570
they dyed their hair and returned to work for us as their own sons.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:43.430
Blessed are you.

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:44.110
Of course they are.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:48.410
Unfortunately for you, Harold, my own eyes are excellent.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.040
You have not only ceased to go forward, you have gone backward.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.800
You have not only stopped progressing, you have stopped thinking.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.540
You not only make the same mistakes year after year,

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:57.920
you don't even change your apologies.

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.000
You have become a butler.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.440
You are the living proof of the low quality of work we demand of our employees

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:08.760
and a bad example to the younger employees who figure that if you can get away with it,

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.980
they can too, they don't have to be any better than you are, which is zero.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:17.980
There are no buts. I have bought you a Swiss watch, 18 carats at Chimes.

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:22.850
It is properly inscribed with gratitude and love and kisses for 20 years,

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:26.910
devoted to service and so forth and so forth, and I herewith present it to you.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.530
Here is also a check that you have.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:38.680
$2,946.12, which, uh, represents your, your, uh, savings deposited with the company.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.460
I'm surprised you haven't saved more in 20 years.

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:45.560
I had a lot more, only it was invested in the preferred stock of the company,

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.900
and you remember what happened in 1929.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.520
Oh, yes, yes, I remember.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.490
Of course, it was just as hard on all of us.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.350
You know, the little and the big, we all shared and shared light,

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.810
but that's all water under the bridge.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.390
Goodbye and good luck.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.000
And as a parting thought, I want you to know that this,

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:07.000
hurting me much more than it is you harold much more thank you very much goodbye don't let it get

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:25.440
you down thank you football it was football i used to play

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.450
- Sorry, Harold.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.860
- Thanks, like that in cash, please.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:45.290
- What's the matter, don't you trust us anymore?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.500
- Once bitten, twice shy.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.600
I'll have to get it out of the safe,

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.760
I'll bring it over to your desk.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.860
- Thank you, Charlie, you better buy a wig.

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:52.950
- Huh? - Why?

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:53.840
- You'll find out.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:03.370
Here you are, Harold.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:07.440
Thanks, Charlie.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.120
Justin Dorsett.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.870
Thanks so long, Charlie.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.000
Might I speak to you?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:05.730
a moment, Miss Otis. Certainly, Mr. Diddlebox. You mean privately? Well, with some privacy.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:09.650
I'd look for something in the private area. I never find anything anywhere.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.460
Splendid. I'll join you in a moment.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:36.340
- Miss Otis, uh-- - Yes, Mr. Diddlebuck.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:40.360
- Miss Otis, when your eldest sister, Hortense,

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:43.460
came to work here some 17 or 18 years ago,

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:44.580
I fell in love with her.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.040
She was a lovely girl.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:47.190
- Yes, I know.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:49.210
I mean that you fell in love with her, she told me.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:52.570
- Oh, she swept me off my feet.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:55.050
My circumstances at that time did not permit

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.610
even the contemplation of marriage.

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.410
- I know, she told.

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:00.000
- When she very wisely said,

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:05.370
stop waiting for me, and marry the gentleman whose life she has since illuminated, I felt

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:10.530
that my own life was ended, that I would never love again, that the sunshine had withdrawn

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:12.570
permanently behind the clouds.

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:13.580
I know.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.580
Well, I was mistaken.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.580
Of course.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.160
Because when your next eldest sister, Irma, came to work here, I fell even more deeply

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:20.920
in love with her than I had with Hortense.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:21.920
I know.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:22.920
She told me.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:23.920
Hortense even got a little burned about it.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.250
Well, she needn't have, because when Irma, in her turn, got married and was replaced

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.000
by your next eldest sister, Harriet.

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:35.640
I felt that everything that had gone before was merely an appetizer.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:36.640
I know.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:37.640
She told me, too.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:39.780
They were getting better and better.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:42.560
Your mother seemed to be making them nicer every year.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:43.560
Thank you.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.300
I haven't come to you yet.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:49.020
When Harriet ran away with that headstone salesman, I was inconsolable.

00:21:49.020 --> 00:21:51.020
None of us felt very good about it.

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:53.340
I was going to propose the very next day.

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:54.600
She didn't know that.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.570
I had the ring in my pocket.

00:21:56.570 --> 00:22:00.000
I just made the last payment on it, the one I'd started for Hortense.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:03.990
I never felt so defeated in my life.

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:08.440
I never thought I'd smile again.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:10.490
She was even better than the others.

00:22:10.490 --> 00:22:12.000
Murder had more practice.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.160
Practice makes perfect.

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:15.900
By then, of course, I'd been wiped out in the market.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:16.990
Was that it?

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:18.150
She never knew.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:19.150
That's right.

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:22.490
I started to get on my feet again when your sister Claire came to work.

00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:23.890
Why didn't you ask her?

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:24.750
Didn't you like her?

00:22:24.750 --> 00:22:26.280
Like her?

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:27.910
I worshipped her.

00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:30.000
Only that irresponsible lout.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.840
loafer who married my sister chose that very moment to kick the bucket with to pass on with

00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:44.420
out leaving even a dime's worth of insurance so i found myself with a ready-made family poor mr

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:49.860
littlebock i suppose you're in love with rosemary too while she was here naturally of course i was

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:53.300
so in the habit of being in love with your mother's daughters but then that it would be

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:57.940
impossible for me to even see one without without without what mr littlebock

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.450
I presume you know I've adored you

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:06.690
since the first morning you punched your first time card.

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:09.110
You knew it, didn't you?

00:23:09.230 --> 00:23:10.900
Well, I suspected it.

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:12.460
My sisters had warned me.

00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:13.600
Of course.

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:18.250
Imagine being exposed to seven Miss Americas

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:20.510
and muffing the whole seven of them.

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:21.600
Poor Mr. Dittle-Dog.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:23.760
Leaving here today.

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:25.040
Oh, no, Mr. Dittle-Dog.

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:26.400
That's what I really wanted to tell you.

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:27.760
I don't know where I'm going,

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.000
and I very probably won't see you again.

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:41.200
just take this. It's all paid for. Someday when you meet some young man who's really worthy of you

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:48.340
and who has everything but the engagement ring, you can take that excuse away from him anyway and

00:25:21.820 --> 00:25:25.120
Confidentially, I left my money on the dresser this morning when I was leaving.

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:29.320
You couldn't let me have four dollars on, I say,

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.700
You couldn't let me have four--

00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:34.380
you couldn't let me have $4 till Wednesday.

00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:35.220
That's my lucky day.

00:25:35.220 --> 00:25:37.480
There's an ad called Futsure running at Belmont.

00:25:37.480 --> 00:25:39.540
And you don't have to go if you can't spare it.

00:25:39.540 --> 00:25:42.140
I just said if you happen to have $4, you wasn't using

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:43.340
until Futsure come in.

00:25:43.340 --> 00:25:45.100
The fool and his money are soon parted.

00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:48.230
Yeah, but think what beautiful memories he lays up.

00:25:48.230 --> 00:25:49.980
How about $2 till tomorrow?

00:25:49.980 --> 00:25:52.360
He who lendeth money endeth friendship.

00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:53.140
Well, that's all right.

00:25:53.140 --> 00:25:54.300
We ain't friends.

00:25:54.300 --> 00:25:56.180
I never even seen you before.

00:25:56.180 --> 00:25:57.840
Well, that's a fine argument.

00:25:57.840 --> 00:25:59.270
How about a quarter for a racing farm?

00:25:59.270 --> 00:26:00.000
This is day before.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.000
Oh, here, since you're so melancholy about yourself.

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:05.400
Fish hooks?

00:26:05.400 --> 00:26:06.280
What?

00:26:06.280 --> 00:26:09.150
I say, maybe you caught your mitt in some fish hooks.

00:26:09.150 --> 00:26:11.290
Holy Moses, Westerner, huh?

00:26:11.290 --> 00:26:17.410
Oh, here, what's the difference?

00:26:17.410 --> 00:26:18.410
Holy mackerel, you're a right guy.

00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:20.410
You stick to me, you'll be wearing rubies.

00:26:20.410 --> 00:26:21.410
No, I'm not.

00:26:21.410 --> 00:26:23.410
It's just that I've been saving it for 20 years,

00:26:23.410 --> 00:26:24.410
and I'm getting tired of it.

00:26:24.410 --> 00:26:25.410
It's what you call an impulse.

00:26:25.410 --> 00:26:28.240
Like a man works all his life in a glass factory,

00:26:28.240 --> 00:26:29.860
well, one day he...

00:26:30.160 --> 00:26:31.660
Feels like picking up a hammer.

00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:33.380
You say you work in a glass factory?

00:26:33.680 --> 00:26:35.080
No, I didn't say that at all.

00:26:35.180 --> 00:26:36.080
It's just...

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:37.260
Oh, well, you wouldn't understand.

00:26:37.840 --> 00:26:39.040
What you needed is a drink.

00:26:39.510 --> 00:26:40.850
Oh, no, I never touch it.

00:26:40.870 --> 00:26:41.450
I never have.

00:26:41.510 --> 00:26:42.930
It runs in my family not true.

00:26:43.010 --> 00:26:43.850
The demon rum...

00:26:43.850 --> 00:26:44.710
Let me tell you what I'm going to do.

