01:15:13.240 --> 01:15:15.360
Hurry up, do something!

01:15:15.360 --> 01:15:16.160
Where are you?

01:15:16.160 --> 01:15:19.020
This thing I can get, I'll hold it.

01:15:19.020 --> 01:15:26.210
There he goes, not everything.

01:15:26.210 --> 01:15:29.420
Mr. Nilbach, hold on a minute.

01:15:29.420 --> 01:15:30.000
Come on.

01:16:38.570 --> 01:16:39.250
Get up, and I...

01:17:35.310 --> 01:17:35.830
Look out!

01:18:00.030 --> 01:18:02.190
Good old Jack, yeah. Good old Jack.

01:18:02.190 --> 01:18:06.450
Was he fond of the plan? No. There was something at it.

01:18:06.450 --> 01:18:10.570
Oh, boy, am I glad something's at it. Oh, boy. Good old Jack.

01:18:10.570 --> 01:18:13.330
Are you sure he's all right, Wormy? Are you all right?

01:18:13.330 --> 01:18:15.000
Are you all right? Good.

01:18:47.720 --> 01:18:50.410
I ain't never gonna be this time again.

01:18:50.410 --> 01:18:53.030
Oh, boy, there's this nice in here.

01:18:53.030 --> 01:18:55.030
Thought you didn't like, Jails.

01:18:55.030 --> 01:18:57.030
This is the first time I ever appreciated one.

01:18:57.030 --> 01:19:00.000
So cozy, so silly.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.310
Don't they build them nice?

01:19:02.310 --> 01:19:04.140
Well, we'll be out of it pretty soon.

01:19:04.140 --> 01:19:05.960
No hurry.

01:19:05.960 --> 01:19:10.350
We got to get over this, you know.

01:19:10.350 --> 01:19:11.350
That wasn't part of the plan at all.

01:19:11.350 --> 01:19:13.340
You're telling me.

01:19:13.340 --> 01:19:14.400
Now, let's see.

01:19:14.400 --> 01:19:16.400
I said that we'd be in jail by 3:30.

01:19:16.400 --> 01:19:18.400
We are, and I love it.

01:19:18.400 --> 01:19:20.400
And out again by a quarter to five.

01:19:20.400 --> 01:19:22.400
We ain't, and it's all right with me.

01:19:22.400 --> 01:19:25.640
Good old Jackie, did you stick your neck out?

01:19:25.640 --> 01:19:27.640
They ought to be here with certified checks.

01:19:27.640 --> 01:19:29.790
Who? The bankers.

01:19:29.790 --> 01:19:30.000
They have to.

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:31.560
They have to come with certified checks.

01:19:31.560 --> 01:19:34.270
There's nothing in this world as strong as a good idea.

01:19:34.270 --> 01:19:35.970
Never has failed, never will fail.

01:19:35.970 --> 01:19:37.290
It cannot fail.

01:19:37.290 --> 01:19:39.050
The thought is planted.

01:19:39.050 --> 01:19:41.150
One more second, they could have planted us, too.

01:19:41.150 --> 01:19:43.540
Can you imagine watching a trapeze act?

01:19:43.540 --> 01:19:47.080
Oh, and the cop, who?

01:19:47.080 --> 01:19:48.320
The bankers.

01:19:48.320 --> 01:19:50.840
Now you just watch, you tend to be indifferent.

01:19:50.840 --> 01:19:58.770
Right, right, right.

01:19:58.770 --> 01:20:00.000
Young lady bailed down.

01:20:00.570 --> 01:20:13.750
a young lady bankers secretary sent her over here come on Mr. Diddlebock I'm so sorry you're in trouble

01:20:13.750 --> 01:20:18.350
why miss Otis that's just Jackie don't pay any attention to him you bailed me out well naturally

01:20:18.350 --> 01:20:22.200
Mr. Diddlebock we just put our savings together that's all he can't get out can't of course not

01:20:22.200 --> 01:20:25.800
that's all savings are for anyway naturally they weren't all mine Hortense had the most of course

01:20:25.800 --> 01:20:30.000
seen the others naturally when we heard you were in trouble are you sure they're strong of course they are they keep me

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:32.160
I can't thank you enough, my dear Miss Otis.

01:20:32.260 --> 01:20:34.300
I'm terribly touched, and as soon as I have a minute,

01:20:34.400 --> 01:20:35.800
I'll thank you for hours.

01:20:35.900 --> 01:20:37.600
But I'm not in the slightest trouble.

01:20:37.700 --> 01:20:40.300
This is all part of a plan, a foolproof plan.

01:20:40.400 --> 01:20:41.340
That cannot fail.

01:20:41.440 --> 01:20:42.440
That cannot fail.

01:20:42.540 --> 01:20:44.340
Oh, I thought you were in trouble.

01:20:44.440 --> 01:20:45.650
Far from it.

01:20:45.750 --> 01:20:47.670
Do I look as if I were in trouble?

01:20:47.770 --> 01:20:49.720
Now, you didn't have to see any bankers downstairs

01:20:49.820 --> 01:20:51.020
on your way up here, did you?

01:20:51.120 --> 01:20:53.020
No, I didn't, Mr. Diddlebock, only a colored man.

01:20:53.120 --> 01:20:53.920
What was he doing?

01:20:54.020 --> 01:20:55.270
Mopping the floor, except the sergeant.

01:20:55.370 --> 01:20:56.830
They've had plenty of time to get here.

01:20:56.930 --> 01:20:58.130
At least one of them should have come

01:20:58.230 --> 01:21:00.000
to steal a march on the others.

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:01.380
They must know where I am.

01:21:01.380 --> 01:21:02.580
The paper says exactly.

01:21:02.580 --> 01:21:04.740
The Battery Park Police Station.

01:21:04.740 --> 01:21:06.560
You didn't have any trouble finding me, did you?

01:21:06.560 --> 01:21:08.130
I didn't see the papers, Mr. Dittlebock.

01:21:08.130 --> 01:21:14.880
Your coachman came and got me.

01:21:14.880 --> 01:21:16.910
Quite as likely as hope, sir.

01:21:16.910 --> 01:21:18.950
And while you was acrobatic-ing this afternoon,

01:21:18.950 --> 01:21:20.350
I would pick you to myself.

01:21:20.350 --> 01:21:27.130
Thanks.

01:21:27.130 --> 01:21:29.380
I'm awfully sorry, Mr. Dittlebock.

01:21:29.380 --> 01:21:30.000
I don't know exactly.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:33.980
But maybe you could get arrested some other time if that's what you're trying to do.

01:21:33.980 --> 01:21:37.980
Well, that's that. But I just can't understand.

01:21:37.980 --> 01:21:41.900
Come on, Wormy. We'll take Miss Otis home anyway.

01:21:41.900 --> 01:21:43.900
That's about all we have to offer.

01:21:43.900 --> 01:21:46.430
And we'll come back and get Jackie in.

01:21:46.430 --> 01:21:52.000
I'd be glad to go back to jail, Miss Otis, if it would get you your savings back.

01:21:52.000 --> 01:21:54.890
Don't talk nonsense, Mr. Dittlebuck. Don't be depressed.

01:21:54.890 --> 01:21:56.710
The day is always dark and so--

01:21:56.710 --> 01:21:58.710
I know. Just before the cyclone.

01:21:58.710 --> 01:21:59.480
I know. Just before the cyclone.

01:22:00.410 --> 01:22:07.330
say what's the battery park police station doing on canal street the battery park police station

01:22:07.330 --> 01:22:11.570
yes that's where the paper said i was oh they couldn't take you in there wasn't room some

