Ringling Brothers Barnum and Bailey?

01:24:54.440 --> 01:24:55.340
You mean for money?

01:24:55.340 --> 01:24:57.180
He certainly didn't buy it for peanuts.

01:24:57.580 --> 01:24:59.600
But I thought that there were some bankers.

01:24:59.660 --> 01:25:00.000
Where's this?

01:25:00.030 --> 01:25:03.210
bankers who wanted it or something oh yes but they didn't want it as much as

01:25:03.210 --> 01:25:05.910
Ringling Brothers Barnum and Bailey wanted it they just wanted it for the

01:25:05.910 --> 01:25:08.790
free circus idea which Mr. Sargent already had which made you a member of

01:25:08.790 --> 01:25:12.630
the firm but Ringling Brothers Barnum and Bailey really wanted it the bankers

01:25:12.630 --> 01:25:15.280
never got any higher than a hundred and fifty thousand dollars hundred and

01:25:15.280 --> 01:25:18.160
fifty thousand dollars that's right but when Ringling Brothers don't like

01:25:18.160 --> 01:25:21.460
something they really don't like it don't like they don't like free circuses

01:25:21.460 --> 01:25:24.100
a hundred and seventy-five thousand dollars worth they don't like them

01:25:24.100 --> 01:25:30.000
hundred and seventy-five thousand I'm so happy for you Mr. Diddlebock I mean so much happened

01:25:30.380 --> 01:25:35.760
such a short time. I'm very proud of you, too. You must be terrible, intelligent. I beg your

01:25:35.760 --> 01:25:44.080
pardon, Mr. Littleback. 175,000. That's right. You see, it's written, oh, it's written twice.

01:25:45.760 --> 01:25:53.590
Oh, you're wearing it. The engagement ring. I remember now, 175,000. How beautiful it

01:25:53.590 --> 01:25:57.430
looks on your little hand. 175,000.

01:26:13.120 --> 01:26:15.010
- What's the matter, Mr. Niddlebock?

01:26:15.010 --> 01:26:17.400
- This ought to be the happiest day of my life.

01:26:17.400 --> 01:26:20.290
The unexpected job, the unexpected money.

01:26:20.290 --> 01:26:22.300
But it isn't funny, isn't it?

01:26:22.300 --> 01:26:24.610
- I'm not quite sure I understand, Mr. Niddlebock.

01:26:24.610 --> 01:26:26.250
- What's so difficult to understand about it?

01:26:26.250 --> 01:26:28.750
I just said that I'm very happy for you.

01:26:28.750 --> 01:26:30.000
If I didn't say it, I meant it.

01:26:30.120 --> 01:26:31.800
just made a killing in circuses.

01:26:31.800 --> 01:26:34.960
I am, you tell me, a member of a large advertising firm

01:26:34.960 --> 01:26:36.520
and I don't know how much per year.

01:26:36.520 --> 01:26:39.920
If ever I could afford to support a, it's just now.

01:26:39.920 --> 01:26:42.650
And again, I've just lost one of the little girls in the world.

01:26:42.650 --> 01:26:43.310
The last one.

01:26:43.310 --> 01:26:45.450
I am naturally delighted.

01:26:45.450 --> 01:26:47.390
Excuse me for even thinking like this.

01:26:47.390 --> 01:26:50.130
Now, if you tell me where you live, I'll take you home.

01:26:50.130 --> 01:26:51.810
You mean you don't remember, Mr. Dittleton?

01:26:51.810 --> 01:26:52.550
Remember what?

01:26:52.550 --> 01:26:53.630
