01:27:25.270 --> 01:27:26.070
Am I sure?

01:27:26.400 --> 01:27:27.580
Really, Mr. Diddlebock?

01:27:27.580 --> 01:27:29.250
This is terrible, Miss Otis.

01:27:29.290 --> 01:27:30.000
I'll never forgive me.

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:33.300
If I live to be to be, I mean, the difference in our age alone is.

01:27:33.300 --> 01:27:36.800
I mean to say, not that I don't worship the very ground you walk on,

01:27:36.800 --> 01:27:38.800
but I mean looking at us together.

01:27:38.800 --> 01:27:40.800
I must have been out of my mind.

01:27:40.800 --> 01:27:41.800
I was out of my mind.

01:27:41.800 --> 01:27:43.300
Why didn't you resist me, Miss Otis?

01:27:43.300 --> 01:27:44.800
Because you were irresistible.

01:27:44.800 --> 01:27:46.800
Irresistible, irresistible.

01:27:46.800 --> 01:27:49.400
My grandmother's poodle, I mean to say, look at me.

01:27:49.400 --> 01:27:50.600
I'm looking at you, ma'am.

01:27:50.600 --> 01:27:51.740
What do you see?

01:27:51.740 --> 01:27:52.240
Husband.

01:27:52.240 --> 01:27:55.740
Your husband, piffle, bunk, sentimental, drip plant.

01:27:55.740 --> 01:27:58.550
Fortunately, there's still time to rectify this nonsense,

01:27:58.550 --> 01:28:00.000
this miscarriage of a...

01:28:00.160 --> 01:28:02.360
I don't think that would be practical, Mr. Diddlebock.

01:28:02.360 --> 01:28:05.660
All right, then you can go to Reno or any place else that you like.

01:28:05.660 --> 01:28:07.160
At least I can afford it now.

01:28:07.160 --> 01:28:08.160
What do you mean it wouldn't be practical?

01:28:08.160 --> 01:28:13.080
I'll always be glad to look after you as generously and as well as I know how.

01:28:13.080 --> 01:28:16.430
Anything that I have is yours, Miss Otis.

01:28:16.430 --> 01:28:19.420
Everything I have is yours, Mr. Diddlebock.

01:28:19.420 --> 01:28:21.880
And I'll tell you something else, Mr. Diddlebock.

01:28:21.880 --> 01:28:23.880
I'm not going to Reno or any place else.

01:28:23.880 --> 01:28:27.880
Because you see, Mr. Diddlebock, it took you so long to make up your mind and join our family.

01:28:27.880 --> 01:28:30.000
That now that we've done it, Mr. Diddlebock.

01:28:30.190 --> 01:28:32.950
We don't think we'd better ever let you go.

01:28:32.950 --> 01:28:34.870
- But my dear Miss Missus.

01:28:34.870 --> 01:28:36.990
- And I'll tell you something else, Mr. Dittlebunk,

01:28:36.990 --> 01:28:39.520
that you also haven't bothered to ask me.

01:28:39.520 --> 01:28:42.530
I love you, Mr. Dittlebunk.

01:28:42.530 --> 01:28:46.810
- My dear Miss Otis, I, I, I, my dear childhood.

01:28:46.810 --> 01:28:52.240
Oh, my dear.

01:29:04.570 --> 01:29:08.130
It must be what I was doing all day Wednesday.
